{"name": "Ashame", "type": "spell", "img": "icons/environment/settlement/temple-night.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>At a location within range, you create the shining, powerful, and intimidating image of your deity.  Each creature within 40ft of this point that can see the image must make a Presence (Save) check.  On failure, the creature takes 2d10 radiant damage.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If the creature has stolen something, injured another creature, or had rolled a Presence (Deception) or Presence (Intimidation) check within the last 24 hours, the creature also takes an additional 2d10 radiant damage and becomes @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.UK95BQ45TGSD5Q3V]{Frightened} for the duration.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;On success in either situation, the creature takes half damage and is not frightened. </p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "level": "5", "charge": false, "school": "abj", "components": {"somatic": true, "verbal": true, "material": true, "ritual": false, "concentration": true}, "materials": {"value": "a holy symbol", "consumed": false, "cost": "", "supply": 0}, "attribute": "spell", "actionType": "save", "activation": {"type": "action", "cost": "1", "condition": ""}, "duration": {"value": "1", "units": "minute"}, "range": {"value": "60", "long": null, "units": "ft"}, "target": {"value": "40", "width": null, "units": "ft", "type": "sphere"}, "damage": {"parts": [["2d10", "radiant"], ["2d10", "additional radiant"]], "versatile": ""}, "save": {"attribute": "pre", "dc": null, "scaling": "spell"}, "showInAttacks": false}, "_id": "N2ZSVB7D1W068EWZ", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Greater Cure", "type": "spell", "img": "icons/magic/life/heart-hand-gold-green-light.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You imbue a creature with immense positive energy, reversing debilitating effects that most other spells cannot cure. This spell does one of the following effects to the target:</p><ul><li>All stacks of @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.R54LQEKSDXNQ3N75]{Bleeding}.</li><li>Remove an effect reducing the target&rsquo;s hit point or attribute maximum.</li><li>@Compendium[undertaking.conditions.HFC5771FPBA3Z870]{Stableize} and remove all of their failed Death Throws.</li><li>Cure <strong>Short-Term Insanity</strong>.</li><li>Reduce @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.ERBR3AG01H4N1L91]{Exhaustion} by 1 level. This spell cannot be cast again until your next long rest.</li><li>You cast @Compendium[undertaking.spells-level-2.N04H7KQXVXSTATL9]{Lesser Cure} on the target.</li></ul><p>Charge: This spell can be Charged, modifying its effects for a cost:&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Diamond Dust worth 100gp: Greater Cure has the additional following effects to choose from:</li><ul><li>Remove one <strong>curse</strong>.</li><li>Unattune one magic item, even cursed items.</li><li>Reduce @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.ERBR3AG01H4N1L91]{Exhaustion} by 1 level.</li><li>Remove @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.AKLQGCY7ULVB4B64]{Petrified}.</li><li>Remove @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.SRRBLPRSJWGUR551]{Poisoned}.</li><li>Trade <strong>Indefinite Insanity</strong> for <strong>Long-Term Insanity</strong> with the same symptoms.</li><li>Trade <strong>Long-Term Insanity</strong> for <strong>Short-Term Insanity</strong> with the same symptoms.</li></ul></ul>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "level": "5", "charge": false, "school": "abj", "components": {"somatic": true, "verbal": true, "material": false, "ritual": false, "concentration": false}, "materials": {"value": "", "consumed": false, "cost": "", "supply": 0}, "attribute": "spell", "actionType": "util", "activation": {"type": "action", "cost": "1", "condition": ""}, "duration": {"value": "", "units": "inst"}, "range": {"value": "0", "long": null, "units": "touch"}, "target": {"value": "1", "width": null, "units": "", "type": "creature"}, "damage": {"parts": [], "versatile": ""}, "save": {"attribute": "", "dc": null, "scaling": "spell"}, "showInAttacks": false}, "_id": "QPM2ECCAG51FC9FW", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Kinetic Burst", "type": "spell", "img": "icons/magic/sonic/projectile-sound-rings-wave.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>With a single motion you fling an enormous amount of mental power outwards in an attempt to throw others backward.  Each creature within a 20 foot cube, originating from you, must make a Strength (Save) check.  On a failed throw, the creature is hurled 30 feet away from you, is knocked prone, and takes 8d6 force damage.  A successful (Save) check causes a creature to take half as much damage, they are not knocked @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.RK3DF56CKMQUV6DM]{Prone}, and they are only moved 5 feet.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;In addition, any unsecured objects within range of the area of effect are automatically thrown 30 feet away. </p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "level": "5", "charge": false, "school": "evo", "components": {"somatic": true, "verbal": true, "material": false, "ritual": false, "concentration": false}, "materials": {"value": "", "consumed": false, "cost": "", "supply": 0}, "attribute": "spell", "actionType": "save", "activation": {"type": "action", "cost": "1", "condition": ""}, "duration": {"value": "", "units": "inst"}, "range": {"value": "0", "long": null, "units": "self"}, "target": {"value": "20", "width": null, "units": "ft", "type": "cube"}, "damage": {"parts": [["8d6", "force"]], "versatile": ""}, "save": {"attribute": "str", "dc": null, "scaling": "spell"}, "showInAttacks": false}, "_id": "RS1WH90WHNO7H1AR", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Mind Shackle", "type": "spell", "img": "icons/magic/control/control-influence-puppet.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>With a wave of your hands you attempt to force a humanoid that you can see within range to submit to your authority.  The humanoid must make a Wisdom (Save) check, and on a failure it is @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.KJXJ0T5RPNC51N4V]{Charmed} by you for the duration.  Should you, or the creatures that are friendly to you, be fighting the target, it gets advantage on the (Save) check.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;While the target is @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.KJXJ0T5RPNC51N4V]{Charmed}, you have a telepathic link with it as long as the two of you are on the same plane of existence.  You can use this telepathic link to issue commands and orders to the creature while you are conscious (no action required).  The target will do its best to obey these orders.  You can give simplistic or general course of action this way, such as \u2018attack that person/creature\u2019, \u2018go into that corner\u2019, or \u2018grab that object\u2019.  If the creature completes an order and it doesn\u2019t receive any further directions from you, it will defend and preserve its own life to the best of its ability, but nothing further.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If you would like to give a more complex and precise order, you can take an action to exert more directed control over the target.  Until the end of your next turn, the creature takes only the actions you choose, and doesn\u2019t do anything that you don\u2019t allow it to do.  During that time you can also have the @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.KJXJ0T5RPNC51N4V]{Charmed} creature use its reaction, at the cost of your own reaction.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Each time the target takes damage, it makes a new Wisdom (Save) check against the spell.  Should it pass the save, then the effects of the spell end.  <br><br>Charge: This spell can be Charged to have a longer duration <ul><li>2 mana: Concentration can be held for 1 hour</li><li>4 mana: Concentration can be held for 8 hours</li></ul></p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "level": "5", "charge": true, "school": "mes", "components": {"somatic": true, "verbal": true, "material": false, "ritual": false, "concentration": true}, "materials": {"value": "", "consumed": false, "cost": "", "supply": 0}, "attribute": "spell", "actionType": "save", "activation": {"type": "action", "cost": "1", "condition": ""}, "duration": {"value": "1", "units": "minute"}, "range": {"value": "60", "long": null, "units": "ft"}, "target": {"value": "1", "width": null, "units": "", "type": "creature"}, "damage": {"parts": [], "versatile": ""}, "save": {"attribute": "wis", "dc": null, "scaling": "spell"}, "showInAttacks": false}, "_id": "84PCT6JT8D1G6SN4", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Noxious Wave", "type": "spell", "img": "icons/magic/acid/dissolve-pool-bubbles.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>A cloud infused with the powers of death bursts out from you and causes those who breathe it to begin to rot from the inside.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;A cloud of gas spreads out in a 30 foot radius around you.  Each creature that you choose, that is hit by the cloud, must make a Constitution (Save) check.  On a failed (Save) check, a creature takes 3d6 poison damage, as well as 3d6 necrotic damage, and is @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.9X088PM7H5U2S1HQ]{Sickened}.  On a success the creature takes half damage and is not @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.9X088PM7H5U2S1HQ]{Sickened}.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The gas cloud stays active up to 1 minute if the caster concentrates to keep it going, but stays stationary.  Creatures that pass through the cloud, or end their turn within it, must make a Constitution (Save) check.  On a success, nothing happens and they pass through it without harm.  On a failure, creatures suffer 2d6 poison damage and 1d6 necrotic damage.  Additionally, should a creature that was @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.9X088PM7H5U2S1HQ]{Sickened} fail a Constitution (Save) check against this effect, they become @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.SRRBLPRSJWGUR551]{Poisoned}.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "level": "5", "charge": false, "school": "nec", "components": {"somatic": false, "verbal": true, "material": false, "ritual": false, "concentration": true}, "materials": {"value": "", "consumed": false, "cost": "", "supply": 0}, "attribute": "spell", "actionType": "save", "activation": {"type": "action", "cost": "1", "condition": ""}, "duration": {"value": "1", "units": "minute"}, "range": {"value": "0", "long": null, "units": "self"}, "target": {"value": "30", "width": null, "units": "ft", "type": "sphere"}, "damage": {"parts": [["3d6", "poison"]], "versatile": ""}, "save": {"attribute": "con", "dc": null, "scaling": "spell"}, "showInAttacks": false}, "_id": "XMHUH8GHDDFKWRSS", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Reincarnate", "type": "spell", "img": "icons/magic/holy/angel-winged-humanoid-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Touching an intact corpse no older than a week, you can take a wandering soul and bring the body back to life, retaining all of its attributes and racial traits, but with this mismatched soul as its owner. The soul generally remembers its previous life and skills, but has missing spots in its memory, and retains some memories of their new body&rsquo;s previous life and skills. If its overall level or challenge rating was higher than your level, they are lowered to no higher than the player&rsquo;s level.</p><p>The sudden change of form and mental attributes, especially for the less sapient, can be either a supremely horrifying or aggrandizing experience. In either case, an extreme reaction is common. However, the creature is also magically @Compendium[undertaking.conditions.KJXJ0T5RPNC51N4V]{Charmed} by you for the next 24 hours, and is likely to do what is asked of them once calmed down.</p><p>The GM determines what kind of soul now inhabits the body. However, the following roll tables may assist them.</p><p><em>Past Life</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>1d100</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Past Life</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>1</p></td><td><p>A deeply malevolent being</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>2-5</p></td><td><p>Demon, Devil, or other Fiend</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>6-20</p></td><td><p>Insect, Worm, or Mollusk</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>21-22</p></td><td><p>Aberration</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>23-25</p></td><td><p>Fey</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>26-30</p></td><td><p>Sentient Plant</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>26-40</p></td><td><p>Fish or Amphibian</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>41-45</p></td><td><p>Elemental</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>46-60</p></td><td><p>Reptile or Avian</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>61-75</p></td><td><p>Beast</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>76-90</p></td><td><p>A Sapient Race; roll on <em>Random Race</em> chart below.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>91-95</p></td><td><p>Dragon</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>96-99</p></td><td><p>Celestial</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>100</p></td><td><p>A being of your choice that&rsquo;s been dead no longer than 10 days.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p><em>Reincarnation Quirk</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>1d20</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Reincarnation Quirk</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>1</p></td><td><p>Two souls sharing a body; roll on the Past Life table and Reincarnation Quirk tables again.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>2</p></td><td><p>Greater Insanity: 2 types of Permanent Insanity</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>3</p></td><td><p>Insanity: 1 type of Permanent Insanity</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>4-8</p></td><td><p>Partial Incompatibility: Permanent -3 to a random attribute</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>9-10</p></td><td><p>Mental Blender: Their identity is partially blended with that of the previous body&rsquo;s owner.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>11-16</p></td><td><p>Total Amnesia: Memories of their past life sometimes come to them in dreams or as a reaction to sudden memories.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>17-19</p></td><td><p>No side effects.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>20</p></td><td><p>Total Compatibility: Permanent +2 to all attributes as the body fits the soul even better than their last.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p>Charge: This spell can be Charged, modifying its effects for a cost:&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Various minerals, metals, and water worth 1,000gp: Trigger the <strong>True Reincarnate</strong> effect below.</li></ul><p><strong>True Reincarnate</strong></p><p>Touching a piece of a dead creature, you attempt to find the creature&rsquo;s soul to bring back to life in a new body.</p><p>Provided that the creature has been dead for no longer than 10 days, the spell forms a new adult body from the material components and calls for the soul to enter that body. If the target&rsquo;s soul is free and willing to do so, the soul can enter into the body and take control of it, otherwise the spell fails and the body instantly decays, but the material component is returned.</p><p>The body is fashioned from this spell by calling upon a deity, nature, spirits, or the world itself to help meld the body, and as such is unstable until the soul enters it, meaning that the body&rsquo;s final form is out of your control, causing the creature&rsquo;s final form to be seemingly random. The GM may choose a form that best suits the will of the force which you called upon when casting the spell, or may roll for the result on the <em>Random Race</em> table. If so, the GM counts how many core races are available in this campaign and lines them up in alphabetical order on the following table, and then adds one more result. The GM then rolls on the table twice with the smallest die that can fit all the player races + 1, and rerolls if the result is empty.</p><p><em>Random Race</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>1d??</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Race</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>1</p></td><td><p><em>*Race 1*</em></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>2</p></td><td><p><em>*Race 2*</em></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>3</p></td><td><p><em>*Race 3*</em></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>...</p></td><td><p>...</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Max Roll</p></td><td><p>Re-roll twice more on this table, taking excess results to be extra branch races applied to the new body</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p>The first roll determines the body&rsquo;s core race. The second roll determines the body&rsquo;s branch race; make an alphabetical table of all of that race&rsquo;s branches and roll to determine which branch race the new body has. Due to the chaotic nature of the spell, racial compatibility is irrelevant.</p><p>The reincarnated creature recalls its former life and experiences, retains its capabilities it had in its original form, but exchanges its original racial traits. If the creature was not originally a sapient race, additionally roll once on the <em>Reincarnation Quirk</em> table.</p><p>Finally, roll on the following table 3 times, reducing the rolled attribute by 1 each time. Then repeat the roll to increase those attributes by 1 each time.</p><p><em>Random Attribute</em></p><table><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>1d6</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Attribute</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>1</p></td><td><p><em>Strength</em></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>2</p></td><td><p><em>Dexterity</em></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>3</p></td><td><p><em>Constitution</em></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>4</p></td><td><p>Intelligence</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>5</p></td><td><p>Wisdom</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>6</p></td><td><p>Presence</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p>&nbsp;</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "level": "5", "charge": false, "school": "tra", "components": {"somatic": true, "verbal": true, "material": false, "ritual": false, "concentration": false}, "materials": {"value": "", "consumed": false, "cost": "", "supply": 0}, "attribute": "spell", "actionType": "util", "activation": {"type": "hour", "cost": "1", "condition": ""}, "duration": {"value": "", "units": "inst"}, "range": {"value": "0", "long": null, "units": "touch"}, "target": {"value": "1", "width": null, "units": "", "type": "creature"}, "damage": {"parts": [], "versatile": ""}, "save": {"attribute": "", "dc": null, "scaling": "spell"}, "showInAttacks": false}, "_id": "LAT1CHJ5SCDL566O", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Telekinetic Might", "type": "spell", "img": "icons/magic/control/buff-strength-muscle-damage-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You force your will upon your surroundings and can manipulate the physical world with your mental power.  When you cast this spell, and as an action each round for the duration, you can exert your will on one creature or object that you can see within range, causing the effects described below for the appropriate target.  You can affect the same target round after round, or choose a new one at any time during the duration.  If you switch targets, the prior target is no longer affected by the spell.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Creature: Using this spell you can try to move up to a Huge or smaller creature.  To do so, make a skill check with your spellcasting ability contested by the creature\u2019s Strength check.  If you win the contest, you can move the creature up to 30 feet in any direction, including upwards, though you cannot move them further away from yourself than the range of the spell would allow.  Until the end of your next turn, the creature is restrained in your telekinetic grip.  If you lift the creature upwards, it is also suspended in mid-air.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;On subsequent rounds, you can use your action to attempt to maintain your telekinetic grip by repeating the contest described above.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Object: You can also attempt to move an object up to 1000 pounds.  If the object is unattended (not being worn or carried) then you automatically move it up to 30 feet in any direction, but not beyond the reach of the spell.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If the object is on someone\u2019s person, or being carried or held, you must make a skill check using your spellcasting ability against the creature\u2019s Strength check.  If you succeed, you can move the object up to 30 feet in any direction so long as it does not go beyond the range of the spell.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;As well, you have fine control over objects in your telekinetic grip.  Meaning you can do things such as manipulating a simple tool, opening a door, stowing or retrieving an item, or pouring out the contents of a vial.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "level": "5", "charge": false, "school": "evo", "components": {"somatic": true, "verbal": true, "material": false, "ritual": false, "concentration": true}, "materials": {"value": "", "consumed": false, "cost": "", "supply": 0}, "attribute": "spell", "actionType": "util", "activation": {"type": "action", "cost": "1", "condition": ""}, "duration": {"value": "10", "units": "minute"}, "range": {"value": "30", "long": null, "units": "ft"}, "target": {"value": "1", "width": null, "units": "", "type": "object"}, "damage": {"parts": [], "versatile": ""}, "save": {"attribute": "", "dc": null, "scaling": "spell"}, "showInAttacks": false}, "_id": "LE5BM8DCSZCPUGMV", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Telepathic Network", "type": "spell", "img": "icons/skills/wounds/anatomy-organ-brain-pink-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>You build a telepathic link among up to eight willing creatures of your choice within range that you can see, forging a psychic bond between each creature to all the others for the duration.  Creatures with an Intelligence score of 2 or less are not affected by this spell.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The targets can communicate telepathically through the forged link whether they share a common language or not, for as long as the spell lasts.  This communication is possible over any distance, however, it does not stretch across planes.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "level": "5", "charge": false, "school": "div", "components": {"somatic": true, "verbal": true, "material": true, "ritual": false, "concentration": false}, "materials": {"value": "a piece of thread with eight knots tied in it", "consumed": false, "cost": "", "supply": 0}, "attribute": "spell", "actionType": "util", "activation": {"type": "action", "cost": "1", "condition": ""}, "duration": {"value": "1", "units": "hour"}, "range": {"value": "30", "long": null, "units": "ft"}, "target": {"value": "8", "width": null, "units": "", "type": "creature"}, "damage": {"parts": [], "versatile": ""}, "save": {"attribute": "", "dc": null, "scaling": "spell"}, "showInAttacks": false}, "_id": "J9QLMOBH6NXLN5OQ", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Unnatural Recovery", "type": "spell", "img": "icons/skills/wounds/blood-cells-vessel-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Pulsing magic through your systems, your natural healing abilities kick in faster and more notably than expected.  The target may immediately spend 1 hit die to restore their hit points.  At the start of each of their subsequent turns for the duration, they restore an additional 1d4 hit points.  <br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If the spell lasts its full duration, the target can regain the hit die it spent as part of this spell.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "level": "5", "charge": false, "school": "nec", "components": {"somatic": true, "verbal": false, "material": true, "ritual": false, "concentration": true}, "materials": {"value": "1 vial of juice", "consumed": false, "cost": "", "supply": 0}, "attribute": "spell", "actionType": "heal", "activation": {"type": "action", "cost": "1", "condition": ""}, "duration": {"value": "1", "units": "minute"}, "range": {"value": "0", "long": null, "units": "touch"}, "target": {"value": "1", "width": null, "units": "", "type": "creature"}, "damage": {"parts": [["1d4", "healing"]], "versatile": ""}, "save": {"attribute": "", "dc": null, "scaling": "spell"}, "showInAttacks": false}, "_id": "IGNKJCNA0BXYD1OT", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
